{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Decision: the docs were wrong; release.yml keeps creating lightweight tags. Reasoning: release provenance comes from PEP 740 attestations signed by the Trusted Publishing OIDC identity plus GitHub immutable releases (enabled: gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/immutable-releases returns enabled=true). An unsigned annotated tag adds only a tagger name/date/message written by the workflow bot, which nothing can verify, while needing an extra privileged git-objects write in the post-publish job. If tags ever need to be verifiable they must be signed. docs/releasing.md \"Tag signing — SKIPPED (lightweight tags + attestations instead)\" now says this, and the RC-safety note is reworded for the dispatch-only trigger (inputs.version). Test: test_docs_tag_type_matches_workflow. Portability: docs and a text test only."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795035185159069624,"uuid":"4d95bd68-027d-4d70-a10f-d177bf6dfbfc"}